    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (71.83) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.24) leading the offensive charge. **Yordan Alvarez** remains our most reliable anchor, benefiting from an elite .421 xwOBA and a favorable matchup against Jack Leiter. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** earns a massive boost due to his elite speed and the \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor against Sean Burke, which creates a prime window for stolen base opportunities\u2014our scarcest category. **Junior Caminero** (65.41) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) also provide substantial value; **Casey Schmitt** specifically sees his score surge past the 60-threshold thanks to a confluence of park factors and a favorable 4.48 xERA from Aaron Civale that allows him to exploit the platoon advantage.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of the \"Lineup Pending\" status across our roster. While **Christian Yelich** (61.55) projects well despite facing a tough arm in Joe Ryan, we are closely monitoring the weather, as the \"Wind Out\" report is the only reason he and **Gary Sanchez** (45.20) remain viable starts against such high-caliber pitching. The most difficult personnel decision involved leaving **Caleb Durbin** (50.85) on the bench; while his speed profile is tempting, the optimizer favored the structural lineup placement of **Hyeseong Kim** (59.60) and **Luke Raley** (60.21), whose platoon advantages and mid-order protections outweighed the slightly lower pure projection of the reserves. We continue to hold **Zac Veen** in our minor league affiliate, as he remains ineligible for active duty until he clears his current roster status.",
